                                                "sense_id": "71c9e131-3e7b-3fb1-a4aa-46f0044607e1",
                                                "text": "“I almost ran away.” / “But you didn’t,” Hallie said seriously. / “We stayed for birthday cake.” Portia sat cross-legged on the bed. “Alfonso’s niece was afraid of the candles and Alfonso helped her blow them out.[…]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "76912f7c-207a-4897-9cd9-4cc1c7ce7e14",
                                                "sense_id": "71c9e131-3e7b-3fb1-a4aa-46f0044607e1",
                                                "text": "We sit around chatting, with plates of birthday cake on our laps that none of us have got the stomach for."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51ae8bda-6eb1-31cf-a299-3c847c84c2c8",
                                        "entry_id": "673fcbf3-1bc8-398e-a157-a699a1a6339f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In particular, a buttery, frosted vanilla cake of the sort commonly made to celebrate birthdays in the US, used in compound words to attribute a buttery or creamy, sugary, vanilla cake flavour or aroma to other things."
                                        ],
